(FMT-24 — the ASSIGNMENT half of "Format Strings as Values": a format
 string works as `Set <text> to "{...}"`, not just as an initializer.
 LANGUAGE.md:3424-3427. Verified rather than merely emitted: the second
 Set reads the counter's value AFTER it changed, so a leaf that only
 exercised the initializer form (the existing gap) could not catch a
 compiler that quietly kept the ORIGINAL format-string value on
 reassignment.
